[
{
"text": "Sailors feared the monster Scylla.",
"s": 0.185,
"e": 1.99,
"hl": [
3
]
},
{
"text": "None knew who made her:",
"s": 2.2,
"e": 3.2,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "a lonely girl with a basket of flowers.",
"s": 3.2,
"e": 5.689,
"hl": [
7
]
},
{
"text": "The Greek gods ruled the world,",
"s": 5.931,
"e": 7.24,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "and played with mortals like toys.",
"s": 7.24,
"e": 9.525,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "Yellow flowers grew",
"s": 9.525,
"e": 10.44,
"hl": [
1
]
},
{
"text": "where Titan blood had soaked the earth.",
"s": 10.44,
"e": 12.33,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "Their sap could change",
"s": 12.56,
"e": 13.42,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "a creature into its truest self.",
"s": 13.42,
"e": 15.15,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "Circe, daughter of the sun god,",
"s": 15.15,
"e": 16.84,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "was mocked by her own family.",
"s": 16.84,
"e": 18.643,
"hl": [
4
]
},
{
"text": "Then she met Glaucos,",
"s": 18.643,
"e": 19.92,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "a poor fisherman who was kind to her.",
"s": 19.92,
"e": 21.758,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "To keep him, she fed him the sap.",
"s": 21.758,
"e": 23.44,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "He became a sea god.",
"s": 23.44,
"e": 24.728,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "A god had no use for Circe.",
"s": 24.728,
"e": 26.64,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "He chose Scylla, a beautiful nymph,",
"s": 26.64,
"e": 28.56,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "who flaunted his gifts.",
"s": 28.56,
"e": 30.12,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "That night, Circe poured",
"s": 30.12,
"e": 31.2,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "the sap into Scylla's bathing pool,",
"s": 31.2,
"e": 32.88,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "to show the world how ugly",
"s": 32.88,
"e": 34.46,
"hl": [
5
]
},
{
"text": "she was inside.",
"s": 34.46,
"e": 35.64,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "Scylla screamed.",
"s": 35.879,
"e": 36.73,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "Six necks burst from the water,",
"s": 37.18,
"e": 38.56,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "six mouths, forever hungry.",
"s": 38.56,
"e": 40.205,
"hl": [
3
]
},
{
"text": "From a cliff above the sea,",
"s": 40.437,
"e": 41.78,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "she snatched sailors from passing ships.",
"s": 41.78,
"e": 43.869,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "The gods exiled Circe.",
"s": 43.869,
"e": 45.51,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "Years later, she learned how",
"s": 45.76,
"e": 46.88,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "many men Scylla had eaten.",
"s": 46.88,
"e": 48.328,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "Every one of them was her fault.",
"s": 48.328,
"e": 50.086,
"hl": [
6
]
},
{
"text": "Centuries later, she went back",
"s": 50.086,
"e": 51.68,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "to face what she made.",
"s": 51.68,
"e": 53.153,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "She couldn't undo it.",
"s": 53.153,
"e": 54.1,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "So she turned Scylla to stone,",
"s": 54.1,
"e": 55.8,
"hl": [
5
]
},
{
"text": "the only peace left.",
"s": 55.8,
"e": 57.041,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "Scylla never chose to be a monster.",
"s": 57.475,
"e": 59.23,
"hl": [
6
]
},
{
"text": "Circe did.",
"s": 59.54,
"e": 60.302,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "She wanted the world",
"s": 60.545,
"e": 61.16,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "to see Scylla's true face.",
"s": 61.16,
"e": 62.65,
"hl": []
},
{
"text": "In the end, the flowers showed her own.",
"s": 62.86,
"e": 65.226,
"hl": [
4,
7
]
}
]